# The build context Docker sends to the daemon on every `docker build`.
#
# This directory is 203 MB, and 202 MB of it is `logs/` — Airflow's task logs,
# which grow with every DagRun. The Dockerfile has no COPY at all (it is
# `FROM apache/airflow` plus one `pip install`), so none of it was ever used;
# it was uploaded and thrown away each time.
#
# Keep this list conservative: if a COPY is added later, anything excluded here
# silently will not be there.

# Airflow runtime output — the whole point of this file
logs/

# Local secrets. The image must never be able to bake these in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python build artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
